{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to bind each sensed condition to exactly one safe action. The policy favors move_forward in clear space, uses random_walk only as a secondary clear-space exploration mode, applies directed turns for side/front obstacles, uses a brief backward escape only in dedicated front-obstacle recovery, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use one-shot action states so each enabled controllable leaves the state immediately",
    "Make all specification states total on uncontrollable events",
    "Bias toward forward progress by returning to clear/forward quickly after recovery",
    "Use full_rotate only from a dedicated stuck/last_resort helper state"
  ],
